+
+### Compiler-discovered header inputs
+
+Native C commands request compiler dependency discovery. n2 persists and replays
+that include closure for local incremental builds. Its database is not part of
+the pure global action identity, so actions with discovery metadata are explicitly
+cache-ineligible until global reuse can validate that closure on cold and warm
+builds. Static package/toolchain header inputs alone do not justify reusing a C
+object whose transitive includes can cross package boundaries.
